  "details": "In the spirit of \"If it's not in posted in canny, it doesn't exist\" even though there's very little information that can be provided.\n\nSome people are experiencing instant crashes where the game just shuts down in open beta. It has only happened twice for me.\n\nThe game was not slowing down, stuttering or experiencing anything special before simply shutting down. I thought I might have seen the Unity crash popup for literally 0.1 seconds (I was looking at my OVR toolkit overlay at the time) before I was already in the SteamVR environment and the game and popup were gone. There are no entries in Windows Event Viewer although I'm not sure if there even should be?\n\nIn my case it didn't seem to be anyone using a crasher as both times it has happened to me I joined back to the instance and it was only me who had crashed.\n\nLog from my previous crash: https://pastebin.com/vvgJD7RH. The original log is 135 megabytes probably because I have --log-debug-levels=API enabled, so I had to cut it down to the last minute before the crash.\n\nOther comments from 3 different people in the open beta discord channel:\n\n\"But yeah, 0 warning at all or a slight lag hitch and then VRChat force close to my SteamVR grid playspace I have setup.\"\n\n\"Im having this same issue, its a crash with 0 warning or lag before happening.\"\n\n\"Anyone else havign random Insta Crashes on open beta\n\nwith no crash dump ?\n\nBeen getting one per hour as well as with 1 of my friends, same kind of crash\"",
